About Us &nbsp;

SharkNinja&nbsp;is a global product design and technology company, with a diversified portfolio of 5-star rated lifestyle solutions that positively&nbsp;impact&nbsp;people’s lives in homes around the world. Powered by two trusted, global brands, Shark and Ninja , the company has a proven&nbsp;track record&nbsp;of bringing disruptive innovation to market and developing one consumer product after another has allowed&nbsp;SharkNinja&nbsp;to enter multiple product categories, driving significant growth and market share gains. Headquartered in Needham, Massachusetts with more than&nbsp;4,100&nbsp;associates, the company’s products are sold at key retailers, online and offline, and through distributors around the world.&nbsp;

AI at SharkNinja

At SharkNinja, we’re building an AI-native culture. We’re not waiting for the future; we’re creating it. Our people are expected to experiment boldly, adopt new tools, and continuously raise what’s possible to create meaningful impact for our consumers. If you believe the best way to do your job hasn’t been invented yet, you’ll fit right in.

About Us &nbsp;

<p&

We code, test and support. We specialize in IT outsourcing and work with clients all around the world. Our offices are in: Warsaw (Poland), Manila (Philippines) and Chicago (USA). Right now, we hire over 120 people and this number is still growing! We started in 1997 and in 2022 we celebrate our 25th Anniversary. We Code Success!

That’s our mission. We want everyone who is related to our company to be successful in whatever they choose to do.

About the project:
We are looking for manual testers who would like to join our development team. Their task is to navigate through the modules at our client, from which product prices are collected and processed for marketing purposes.
The project is currently offered on a month-to-month basis, with the possibility of extension depending on the client's needs and project continuation.
Responsibilites:

• As QA Engineer you will be making functional test scenarios;

• You will be conducting manual tests for mobile devices - Both for Android and iOS;

• You will be helping team with reporting bugs;

• You will be performing manual testing for mobile applications;

• You will be performing regression testing;

• You will be executing tests using different methodologies - preferred black/white box methodology;

• You will be collecting and confirming requirements during daily conversations;

• You will be giving feedback about progress of your work.

Requirements:

• 3+ years experience of testing mobile applications;

• Experience with case management tools - preferable Zephyr;

• Experience with Jira and Confluence;

• Ability to work in English;

• Problem-solving attitude;

• Time Management skills;

• Team player personality.

Nice to have:

• Experience with Salesforce;

• ISTQB certificate - Foundation level.

We offer:

• Salary for work amounting to 10 000 - 13 000 zł on B2B;

• Flexible working conditions;

• Private healthcare, Multisport card and trainings.

